# VS Code REST Client / Visual Studio .http file.
# Use the bootstrap admin configured via user-secrets (see README).
# Credentials are read from backend/src/Omnichannel.Api/.env (git-ignored), e.g.:
#   BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=...
#   BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=...
# Never put a real credential in this file.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@email = {{$dotenv BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@password = {{$dotenv BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}

### Health (anonymous)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Validation error (400 ProblemDetails)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": ""
}

### ---- Channel product mappings (task 014) and realtime / dashboard (task 015) ----
# Run "Login" first: the requests below take the token from its response. Ids are placeholders: copy them from the
# responses of "Channels" and "Products" (or set the variables here). No secrets in this file.
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
@channelId = 0199a1b0-0000-7000-8000-000000000002
@productId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@channelProductId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Channels (ids of website / pos / digital-platform)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/channels
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Products (pick a productId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Mappings of a channel (search: SKU, product name, external product id, external SKU)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/channels/{{channelId}}/products?page=1&pageSize=20&sortBy=sku
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Map a product on the channel (Manager/Admin) - 201 with syncTaskId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/channels/{{channelId}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "externalProductId": null,
  "externalSku": "WEB-0001"
}

### One mapping (the Location of the 201)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/channels/{{channelId}}/products/{{channelProductId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change external ids / deactivate a mapping (Manager/Admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/channels/{{channelId}}/products/{{channelProductId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "externalProductId": null,
  "externalSku": "WEB-0002",
  "status": "Active"
}

### Stock-sync tasks of the channel
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/processing/tasks?taskType=StockSync&channelId={{channelId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dashboard summary (default range: the last 24 hours)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dashboard summary for a range (at most 92 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/summary?from=2026-10-01T00:00:00%2B07:00&to=2026-10-02T23:59:59%2B07:00
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---- Alerts (task 017) ----

### Alerts that need attention (default: Open and Acknowledged, most recent occurrence first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Alerts by type and status (both repeatable), most frequent first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/alerts?type=StockSyncFailed&type=ProcessingFailed&status=Open&sortBy=occurrenceCount
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Resolved low-stock alerts of a product, in a range of their last occurrence (at most 92 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/alerts?status=Resolved&type=LowStock&productId={{productId}}&from=2026-10-01T00:00:00%2B07:00&to=2026-10-03T23:59:59%2B07:00
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One alert (pick an alertId from the list)
@alertId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/alerts/{{alertId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Acknowledge an alert (Manager/Admin) - 200 with the alert, 409 alert_resolved, 404 alert_not_found
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/alerts/{{alertId}}/acknowledge
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---- System events / Logs-Audit (task 018b; Manager/Admin, user.* events for an Admin only) ----

### The newest events of the last hours (from only: no upper end)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/system-events?from=2026-10-03T00:00:00%2B07:00
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Errors and warnings of two event types (level and eventType are repeatable), oldest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/system-events?level=Error&level=Warning&eventType=processing.failed&eventType=order.insufficient_stock&sortDir=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Trace: every event of one flow (pick a correlationId from a list answer or from a task)
@eventCorrelationId = 00000000000000000000000000000000
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/system-events?correlationId={{eventCorrelationId}}&sortDir=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Events of a task in a range (at most 92 days when both ends are given)
@eventTaskId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/system-events?taskId={{eventTaskId}}&from=2026-10-01T00:00:00%2B07:00&to=2026-10-03T23:59:59%2B07:00
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### User management audit - an Admin gets the events, a Manager an empty page (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/system-events?eventType=user.created&eventType=user.role_changed&eventType=user.locked
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Realtime hub: negotiate (what a SignalR client does first). 401 without a token.
# A browser passes the token as ?access_token=... on the hub's requests; here the header is used so that no token ends up
# in a URL of this file.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/hubs/notifications/negotiate?negotiateVersion=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---- Product images (task 019; presign / confirm / remove: Manager/Admin) ----
### The bytes never pass through the API: 1. presign, 2. PUT the file to uploadUrl (the storage), 3. confirm.

### 1. A link for one upload (contentType: image/jpeg, image/png or image/webp; sizeBytes: 1 .. 5 MiB)
# @name presign
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}/image/presign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contentType": "image/png",
  "sizeBytes": 20480
}

### 2. The upload itself goes to the storage, NOT to the API: no Authorization header, exactly the Content-Type above.
###    (uploadUrl is a credential for five minutes - never paste it anywhere.)
PUT {{presign.response.body.uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample.png

### 3. Confirm: the stored object is checked (key of this product, size, type, first bytes) and becomes the image.
###    200 with the product (image.url = a download link for 15 minutes); 400 on objectKey; 503 storage_unavailable.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "objectKey": "{{presign.response.body.objectKey}}"
}

### The product with its image (every role; a new image.url with each answer)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Remove the image - 204, also when the product has none
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
